※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4640

※ A parameter written `mut` is an array whose elements the body may write, in
※ the caller's array; one named without `mut`, or one in `⎕static`, may not be
※ written by anyone, and so may not be handed to it.

@[impure]
fn clear(a: mut u8⟦⟧):
    a⟦0⟧ ← 0u8

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let fixed: u8⟦2⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8⟧ in ⎕static
    clear(fixed)
    0u6
